__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"LEGAL",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const o={terms:{title:"Terms of service",updated:"Last updated October 11, 2026",short:["FIG is free for you, and FIG doesn't show ads.","A deal counts once staff scan your QR at the restaurant.","One account per person. No sharing codes or faking visits."],sections:[{heading:"1. Who we are",paragraphs:["FIG is a local deals app based in Markham, Ontario, Canada (\"FIG\", \"we\", \"us\"). These terms cover the FIG app and website. By creating an account, you agree to them and to our Privacy Policy."]},{heading:"2. Your account",paragraphs:["You can look around FIG without an account. To claim deals, order or post, you need one, and you must be 14 or older. If you're under 18, check with a parent or guardian that it's okay. Use your real name, an email and a mobile number, each confirmed with a code. One account per person and per mobile number. Keep your password private. You're responsible for what happens on your account."]},{heading:"3. How deals work",paragraphs:["Deals are offered by restaurants, not by FIG. Each deal shows its own rules (times, limits, dine-in only, and so on) before you claim it.","\u2022 A claimed deal is yours until the restaurant ends the deal, or until a flash or dated deal is over.","\u2022 At the restaurant, open your QR code. It refreshes every 5 minutes.","\u2022 The deal is used once staff scan it. That scan is a \"redemption\".","Restaurants can change or end a deal at any time. A deal isn't guaranteed until staff scan it. Some deals come as takeout: a takeout order always comes with one of those deals, which is applied to it; dine-in only deals can't be. You pay the restaurant in the app or at pickup, whichever it has set up. If you don't collect an order within 2 hours of its pickup time, it shows as a missed pickup on your takeout record (12 months), which restaurants can see when you order. Nobody reports it and takeout is never switched off for it."]},{heading:"4. Play fair",paragraphs:["Restaurants honour every deal in good faith, so we protect them from abuse. Don't:","\u2022 make more than one account","\u2022 share, screenshot or sell QR codes","\u2022 fake visits or redeem without buying","\u2022 use bots, scripts or location spoofing","\u2022 harass restaurant staff or other diners","If we see this, we may cancel claims or suspend your account."]},{heading:"5. Ads",paragraphs:["FIG doesn't show ads. If we add them later, we'll update these terms first. A paid spot would always be labelled Sponsored, and would never change a deal, its price or its reviews."]},{heading:"6. Restaurants and your food",paragraphs:["FIG doesn't run any restaurant. Food, prices, service, safety and allergens are the restaurant's responsibility. Dietary filters are a guide only. Always tell staff about allergies before you order."]},{heading:"7. What you send us",paragraphs:["If you send us photos, reports or feedback, you still own them. You let us use them to run and improve FIG. Don't send anything that isn't yours or breaks the law. Reviews must be about your own scanned visit and honest. They're public under your first name and last initial. We can remove reviews that are abusive, fake or off-topic."]},{heading:"8. Leaving FIG",paragraphs:["You can delete your account anytime in Profile \u2192 Account & password. We can suspend or close accounts that break these terms. If we do, we'll tell you why unless the law or safety stops us."]},{heading:"9. Our responsibility",paragraphs:["We work hard to keep FIG accurate and running, but it's provided \"as is\". As far as the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect losses, and our total liability to you is limited to the greater of what you paid us in the last 12 months or $50 CAD. Nothing here removes your rights under Ontario consumer protection law."]},{heading:"10. Changes to these terms",paragraphs:["If we make an important change, we'll tell you in the app at least 14 days before it starts. If you keep using FIG after that, the new terms apply."]},{heading:"11. Governing law",paragraphs:["These terms are governed by the laws of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. Disputes go to the courts of Ontario."]}],contactAsk:"Questions about these terms?",contactLine:"FIG, Markham, Ontario"},privacy:{title:"Privacy policy",updated:"Last updated October 11, 2026",short:["We collect what we need to show you deals nearby and check that redemptions are real.","We never sell your personal information.","Restaurants only see what they need to verify your visit.","Location is used while you use FIG, and for alerts only if you turn them on.","You can download or delete your data anytime."],sections:[{heading:"1. Who's responsible",paragraphs:["FIG, based in Markham, Ontario, Canada, is responsible for your personal information. We follow Canada's privacy law (PIPEDA). Our Privacy Officer answers questions sent with Message us in the app, or from the contact page at fig-promo.vercel.app/contact."]},{heading:"2. What we collect",paragraphs:["\u2022 Account: name, username, email and mobile number (each confirmed with a code), photo, and your password (stored scrambled, never readable).","\u2022 Taste: cravings, budget, dietary needs and home area from Profile setup.","\u2022 Location: your precise location while you use FIG, to show nearby deals. It's optional: you can find, claim and use every deal with it off. If you tap I'm here on a takeout order, we keep how far you were from the restaurant with that order. If you turn on arrival reminders, also when you arrive at a restaurant where you have a claimed deal.","\u2022 Activity: claims, verified visits, searches, takeout orders, chat messages, and the reviews and photos you post.","\u2022 Device: phone model, app version, notification token and crash reports.","\u2022 Terms: which version of our terms you accepted, and when.","\u2022 Two-step login: if you turn it on, the key that links FIG to your authenticator app. The codes it makes stay on your phone.","\u2022 Support: messages and reports you send us."]},{heading:"3. How we use it",paragraphs:["\u2022 Show deals and places near you","\u2022 Verify redemptions and stop fraud","\u2022 Keep a record of your visits, so you can rate them and find places again","\u2022 Personalise Home (you can turn this off)","\u2022 Send the alerts and emails you chose","\u2022 Deliver chat messages between you and a restaurant. Phone numbers typed into a chat are hidden. The FIG team reads a chat only when someone reports it","\u2022 Answer support requests and improve FIG","FIG doesn't show ads. We don't sell your information or show you third-party ads based on it."]},{heading:"4. Dietary needs",paragraphs:["Dietary needs can say something about your health or beliefs, so we treat them as sensitive. They're only used to filter deals for you. They're never shared with restaurants."]},{heading:"5. What restaurants see",paragraphs:["When staff scan your QR, the restaurant sees your first name and last initial, the deal, and the time. Their dashboard shows totals, like \"42 redemptions this week\", not who you are. Restaurants never see your email, location or history. They never see your mobile number, not even for a takeout order: they reach you by chat or a notification in FIG. Reviews you post are public and show your first name and last initial."]},{heading:"6. Companies that help us",paragraphs:["These companies process data for us, only to run FIG, under contracts that protect it:","\u2022 Supabase: database and sign-in","\u2022 Vercel: hosting","\u2022 Stripe: card payments for takeout orders, and restaurants\u2019 payouts. To set up a restaurant\u2019s payouts, FIG shares its business name, address, phone and email with Stripe. ID and bank details go straight to Stripe and never pass through FIG.","\u2022 Twilio: text messages, like the codes that confirm your mobile number or sign you in","\u2022 Apple and Google: sign-in, maps, notifications"]},{heading:"7. Where your data lives",paragraphs:["Some of these companies store data outside Canada, mostly in the United States. There, it's protected by our contracts but also covered by local law."]},{heading:"8. How long we keep it",paragraphs:["We keep your data while your account is open. When you delete your account, we erase your personal information within 30 days. We keep nightly backup copies for up to 30 days, so it's gone from those within 30 days too. Redemption records are kept without your name for up to 7 years, because restaurants are billed for them and tax law requires it."]},{heading:"9. Your choices",paragraphs:["\u2022 See or fix your info in Profile","\u2022 Download it in Privacy & terms","\u2022 Turn off location, alerts or personalised picks","\u2022 Delete your account at any time","Not happy with our answer? You can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada."]},{heading:"10. Keeping it safe",paragraphs:["We encrypt data in transit, scramble passwords and limit who on our team can access data. You can turn on two-step login, so signing in also needs a code from an authenticator app. Where it's available, you can sign in with a code we text to your confirmed mobile number instead of a password. No system is perfect. If a breach could put you at risk, we'll tell you and the Privacy Commissioner, as the law requires."]},{heading:"11. Age",paragraphs:["FIG is for people 14 and older. We don't knowingly collect information from anyone younger. If we learn that someone under 14 has an account, we delete it."]},{heading:"12. Changes",paragraphs:["If we change how we use your information in an important way, we'll tell you in the app first, and ask for your consent where the law requires it."]}],contactAsk:"Questions about your privacy?",contactLine:"Privacy Officer, FIG, Markham, Ontario"},"business-terms":{title:"Business terms",updated:"Last updated October 11, 2026",short:["FIG is free: joining, your page, deals, scans and chats. No commission on the bill.","Takeout orders paid in the app: FIG keeps 5% of the food, and Stripe\u2019s card fee comes off the same payment.","FIG Premium is optional: $50 a year, cancel anytime.","Honour your live deals exactly as written.","Only your enrolled staff devices can verify scans."],sections:[{heading:"1. Who these terms are for",paragraphs:["These terms apply to restaurants in Canada that use FIG Business. They sit alongside our Terms of service and Privacy policy. By signing up, you confirm you're 18 or older and can accept them for your business."]},{heading:"2. Your listing",paragraphs:["You must run a real, licensed food business at the address you give us, and keep your details accurate. Your page goes live as soon as you finish setting it up. We can pause or remove a listing that breaks these terms."]},{heading:"3. Your deals",paragraphs:["You choose your deals, times and daily limits. While a deal is live, you must honour it exactly as listed. Don't raise prices to cancel out a discount. If you pause a deal, keep honouring claims made before that. Ending a deal is what stops its claims."]},{heading:"4. What FIG costs",paragraphs:["\u2022 Joining FIG, setting up your page, going live, posting deals, verified scans, chats and up to 2 locations are free. There's no commission on the bill, and no sign-up, monthly, listing or per-scan fees.","\u2022 Takeout orders paid in the app are paid out to you through Stripe. Setting up payouts happens inside FIG, and accepting Stripe\u2019s terms (the Stripe Connected Account Agreement) is part of it. Your ID and bank details go straight to Stripe, never to FIG.","\u2022 When a diner pays for a takeout order in the app, FIG keeps 5% of the food before tax, and Stripe\u2019s card fee (2.9% + $0.30 for most Canadian cards) comes off the same payment. The rest, tax included, is paid out to you, and the tax is yours to remit. A takeout order the diner pays for at your counter has no FIG fee.","\u2022 FIG Premium is optional: $50 CAD a year plus applicable tax, for your whole account and all its locations. It adds unlimited locations, deal announcements (one every 2 hours, to nearby diners whose cravings match your food and to diners who saved you; diners can turn them off), area insights, and a Premium badge that never changes your ranking. It renews yearly until you cancel; cancel anytime in FIG and it stays on until the end of the year you paid for. It's paid by card through Stripe, or, if you buy it through the App Store or Google Play, their payment and refund terms apply."]},{heading:"5. Ads",paragraphs:["FIG doesn't sell ads right now. If we offer them later, it will be under separate terms you agree to first."]},{heading:"6. Wrong scans and disputes",paragraphs:["You can report a scan you think is wrong within 14 days. We review it, and if it was a mistake we remove it."]},{heading:"7. Reviews",paragraphs:["Paying FIG never changes, hides or removes reviews. You can reply to reviews in public. Don't offer anything in exchange for a review."]},{heading:"8. Staff and devices",paragraphs:["You're responsible for scans made by your staff and devices. Remove access when someone leaves."]},{heading:"9. Diner information",paragraphs:["You'll see a diner's first name, last initial and the deal they used, never their mobile number or email. Reach a diner only through FIG (chat, or \"We're waiting\" on a takeout order), and only to serve that deal or order. Don't contact diners outside FIG, and handle their information as Canadian privacy law requires."]},{heading:"10. Ending the agreement",paragraphs:["You can close your business account anytime. Taps up to then are invoiced as usual. We can suspend or close your account if you break these terms, for example by not honouring deals or faking scans. If we close it for any other reason, nothing more is charged."]},{heading:"11. Responsibility",paragraphs:["You're responsible for your food, prices, service and safety, and for any claims about them. FIG is provided \"as is\". As far as the law allows, our total liability is limited to the greater of the fees you paid us in the last 12 months or $100 CAD."]},{heading:"12. Changes and law",paragraphs:["We'll give you at least 30 days' notice before changing the price. A new price applies from your next renewal. These terms follow Ontario law, and disputes go to the courts of Ontario."]}],contactAsk:"Questions about these terms?",contactLine:"FIG, Markham, Ontario"}}},1754,[]);
